 And I am so, so grateful every day to God, who calls me to do better even as he loves me without reserve. I belong entirely to him now. Every day I lay my faults and failures at his feet, and every day he shapes me just a little more into the person he made me to be. It isn't that he changes me, I think; it's that he cleans me, wipes off the grime of my lifelong attempts to run my life myself, so that more of his love courses through me in the way he intended. Sometimes the grime is crusted tight, and the cleaning is hard to take; even then, I know I am his treasured child, and I am eager to delight him. The reins of my life are in his hands, where they belong, and I have never felt more peace and contentment.